// Package sha1dc implements Marc Stevens & Dan Shumow's collision-detecting
// SHA-1 (SHA-1DC, MIT License) wholly in pure Ergo with zero Go externs.
//
// Every 64-byte block runs the 80-round SHA-1 compression while capturing
// intermediate states at steps 58 and 65, evaluates the 32 unavoidable
// bit-condition (UBC) disturbance-vector filters, and recompresses any
// triggered disturbance vector backward and forward to confirm whether a
// near-collision / cryptanalytic collision attack is present. When detected,
// SHA-1DC applies the standard double-recompression safe-hash (matching Git's
// SHA1DC_INIT_SAFE_HASH_DEFAULT = 1) and fails with CollisionDetected carrying
// that 20-byte safe-hash digest.
//
// Hasher is an immutable value type backed by fixed arrays ([5]uint32 and
// [64]byte) so block compression stays allocation-free and every law runs both
// in the check-time evaluator and natively.

// CollisionDetected reports that SHA-1DC detected a cryptanalytic SHA-1
// collision attack on the hashed stream. Digest carries the 20 raw bytes of
// the safe-hash digest produced by SHA-1DC double recompression.
type CollisionDetected {
	Digest string,
}

// Hasher holds the incremental state of a collision-detecting SHA-1 computation.
// Construct with New, feed chunks with Write or WriteString, and finish with
// Digest or DigestString.
type Hasher {
	ihv            [5]uint32,
	total          uint64,
	buf            [64]byte,
	bufLen         int,
	foundCollision bool,
}
